@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Me";
    var emailSubject = Uri.EscapeDataString("About Me Inquery");
}

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">

        <h1 class="h3 mb-4">About Me</h1>

        <p>
            I’m a senior .NET developer with extensive experience building, maintaining,
            and modernizing production applications and APIs. My background includes
            enterprise systems and data-driven applications where reliability, clarity,
            and long-term support are critical.
        </p>

        <p>
            I built this Resume API to move beyond a static resume and instead demonstrate
            how I design and deliver real systems. The application exposes resume data
            through versioned REST endpoints while also providing a simple UI for human readers.
        </p>

        <p>
            Design decisions—such as using a lightweight email entry instead of full
            authentication, storing data in memory only, and recycling the service on an
            automated schedule—reflect how I balance usability, security, and simplicity
            in real-world applications.
        </p>

        <p>
            Throughout my career, I’ve focused on building software that is understandable,
            maintainable, and fit for purpose. I value clear APIs, predictable behavior,
            and pragmatic solutions over unnecessary complexity.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4">
            <p class="mb-2">
                If you’re interested, feel free to explore the API, review the code, or reach out directly.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-4">
                Contact: <a href="mailto:j24hart@gmail.com?subject=@emailSubject">j24hart@gmail.com</a>
            </p>

            <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="/Index">Back to main</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>
